{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/559540-3rd-teaser-question","id":559540,"title":"3rd Teaser Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-18T10:41:18-07:00","id":559540,"title":"3rd Teaser Question","content":"<i>&quot;is it the Caledfwlch-aka-Excalibur of the Welsh Mabinogi, or the hill-cleaving sword of the Irish Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann? At least the other Celtic pantheon can\u2019t lay claim to it. This has been your weekly Scion teaser.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> I guess it is, if you want to. If you want to make up a great new story about the Children of Llyr stealing it after the debacle in Ireland. And then the Tuatha getting it back somehow... Or not. It's probably going to be easier to keep them as separate things. Just because the names are similar doesn't mean they have to be the same thing. Particularly when the languages are closely enough related that the meaning of one and the meaning of the other are going to be similar. <br /> <br /> And of course it doesn't appear in the &quot;third Celtic pantheon&quot; , presumably it's the Gaulish pantheon, so, since all you've got to built it from is some names teased out of place names and records from other peoples. If you don't have a single actual myth story, you are apt not to have any narrative to draw from. So, sure, there could be a third sword or the same sword a third time. (The Celts would probably feel the whole thing was more.... complete.... in such a case.) Just make it up from whole cloth with like 20 threads, all weft, when you make up the rest of the pantheon. I recollect there are definitely some depictions of swords in what are probably mythological contexts on some artifacts and there is definitely PLENTY of cultic evidence for the importance of sowrds at Gaulish cultic sites. So, go at it. &lt;Shrug&gt;<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I guess Mjolnir, Zeus's thunderbolts, Perun's lighting stones and Indra's sword could all be the same thing as well.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:43:07-07:00","id":559867,"title":"","content":"I meant it more as, &quot;Not only are the Tuatha and the Gauls in there, but so are the Welsh, and we're trying to portray pantheons in relation to one another,&quot; but okay then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise, I guess Mjolnir, Zeus's thunderbolts, Perun's lighting stones and Indra's sword could all be the same thing as well.....</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't, as you know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T18:44:07-07:00","id":560175,"title":"","content":"You juxtaposed a sword from Welsh mythology with a sword from Irish mythology then proposed the possibility of conflating them (can't really juxtapose anything with Gaulish mythology... but oh, well... except there is this scene from the Gundestrup Cauldron that harkens to Fergus mac Roich using a chariot wheel as a weapon, but that's close to it...) . You could also do exactly the same with the hammer, the javelins, the spear(?) and the sword. They are all lightning. So perhaps they all came from the same place, some mystic &quot;Well of Lighting&quot; or something.... one was forged into a hammer, another into a spear, another into a sword, and some of the left over arcs into javelins. (Can't you just see a cross-pantheon band of Zeus, Thor, Indra and Perun going off on to seek the Well of Lightning.... back in the long long ago...) How is mashing up the lighting weapons of the thunder gods not the same thing as mashing up a couple of powerful blades into the Bad Ass Sword of Celt-in-dom? It's taking things from related mythologies that are similar and positing that they are, in fact, identical, or, similarly derived. <br /> <br /> I've built whole Scion games around just this exact conceit. You are going to have to do some fast shuffling, but it might work. Which means that the Dagda's cauldron and the cauldron Bran gave to Matholwch (that Efnisien broke) could be the same thing too. You just need a really good story.... Perhaps the plague that killed off the Nemedians is in fact the same plague that wiped out the Irish in the Mabonogi.... so the survivors who sailed to the north took the broken pieces to Tir nan Og with them, then when they returned to Ireland as the Tuatha De, the Dagda brought it back..... (Which also explains that whole thing about Mannanan mac Lir being from an &quot;older pantheon&quot; thing... He IS, because, unlike Lleu and Lugh (who are two totally different people... there's just too much dissimilarities from birth, to life, to death to match them up), Manawyddan and Mannanan actually are 100% the same god. Manannan knows is such a wise, outsider type because he knew the ancestors of the Tuatha when they wore short pants (assuming the gods are wearing the big boy pants). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T13:58:05-07:00","id":568366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"100%\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 3px\"> <span style=\"font-family:courier\"><b><span style=\"color:#F2A400\">DAVESPRITE: oh looks like you got caledfwlch</span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#F2A400\">DAVESPRITE: you found that pretty fast</span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#E00707\">DAVE: is that how you pronounce that</span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#F2A400\">DAVESPRITE: yeah i guess so</span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#F2A400\">DAVESPRITE: i think its welsh</span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#E00707\">DAVE: what are welsh things doing in this game</span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#F2A400\">DAVESPRITE: thats an awesome question</span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#E00707\">DAVE: fuck yeah it is</span> </b></span></td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}